<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n170" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbortus</span></b> , ūs,
			m. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abortum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i><span class="en">Dig. 29, 2,
		30</span></i>; cf. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 29</span></i> Müll.) [aborior],
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an abortion</i>,
				<i>miscarriage.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicam abortum esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Hec. 3, 3, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tertullae nollem abortum,</span>”
				<i>had not miscarried</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 14, 20, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abortum facere,</span>”
				<i>to suffer abortion</i>, <i>miscarry</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 8, 10, 1</span></i>
			; but also, <i>to produce</i> or <i>cause abortion</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 18, 22, § 118</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">21, 18, 69,
				§ 116 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, of plants, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 2,
				6, § 13</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of writings, <i>an
				unfinished piece</i>, Plin. praef. § 28.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
